Something scratched on the window-sill.
A pinched brown face peered in--I shivered;
No one listened or seemed to see;

shines:
Buzz the dull flies on the chamber window;
Brave shines the sun through the freckled pane;
Fearless the cobweb swings from the ceiling --

Her lips curved with a smile:
'Where Margaret shines like the sun
I shine but like a moon;

shine:
Come thou, my compensation, my dear sight,
My morning-star, my morning! rise and shine,
And touch my hills with radiance not their own;

shiver:
When my stark carcass you secretly sank.
Ha, now I see that you tremble and shiver;
'T was but my spirit that passed when you shrank!

ships:
He sifted all the refuse of the town,
Explored the trains, enquired among the ships,
And felt the country through from end to end;

I saw at sea a great fog bank
Between two ships that struck and sank;
A thousand screams the heavens smote;

ship's:
